{
    "background_story": "Annabelle was a rugged and fearless prospector who made her name in the Wild West. She spent her days panning for gold in the dusty gulches of California, braving treacherous terrain and harsh weather conditions. Annabelle's determination and grit earned her the respect of her fellow miners, who nicknamed her 'Gulch Annie.' One day, while exploring a particularly remote gulch, Annabelle stumbled upon a hidden vein of gold. Her discovery sparked a small gold rush, and soon the gulch was teeming with miners. Annabelle's claim became one of the most lucrative in the area, and she used her newfound wealth to establish a thriving mining community. Her legend grew, and Annabelle became a symbol of female empowerment and pioneering spirit in the American West.",
